			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Add Debug state management and TreeView badge support\n\nThis commit introduces significant infrastructure improvements across the Mountain backend:\n\n### New Debug State Module\n- Added `FeatureState::Debug::DebugState` for managing debug provider registrations\n- Implements `DebugConfigurationProviderRegistration` and `DebugAdapterDescriptorFactoryRegistration`\n- Provides thread-safe registration and lookup methods for debug providers\n- Updated `FeatureState::State` to include the new Debug module\n\n### TreeView Badge Support\n- Added `Badge` field to `TreeViewStateDTO` with validation (max 2048 bytes)\n- Implemented `SetBadge()` method with proper length validation\n- Connected badge setting in `TreeViewProvider::UIState::set_tree_view_badge()`\n\n### DebugProvider Integration\n- Removed TODO comments in `DebugProvider.rs`\n- Now stores debug configuration provider registrations in ApplicationState\n- Now stores debug adapter descriptor factory registrations in ApplicationState\n\n### Code Quality Improvements\n- Updated TODO comments to DEPENDENCY comments, clarifying what blocks full implementation\n- Improved DTO deserialization in `CreateEffectForRequest.rs` for InputBoxOptions, OpenDialogOptions, and SaveDialogOptions\n- Added proper error handling with fallbacks to defaults when deserialization fails\n- Consistent formatting across RPC services (SecretStorageService, WindowService, WorkspaceService)\n- Updated Entry.rs comment to reflect implemented async scheme handler delegation\n\n### Impact\nThese changes establish the foundation for debug adapter support and improve type-safe DTO handling throughout the backend.",
			"SHA": "f1064171031f84597f0a7aa8a21ef48eacbfa421"
		},
